# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VivaMama — CODEOWNERS
#
# Every path below requires an approving review from a listed owner before a
# PR can merge into the default branch. Enforced by the "Main Branch Protection"
# ruleset (Settings → Rules → Rulesets) with "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled — without that checkbox this file is advisory only.
#
# Syntax notes, because they bite:
#   * LAST matching pattern wins — not the most specific one. Order here goes
#     broad → narrow, so the security-critical sections at the bottom always
#     take precedence over the catch-all at the top. Adding a broad rule at the
#     end would silently disable everything above it.
#   * Owners must have write access to the repo, or the rule is ignored.
#   * A pattern that matches nothing fails silently. Verify with
#     `git ls-files <path>` before adding one.
#   * A code owner cannot approve their own PR. Keep at least two owners on
#     every security-critical path so neither maintainer is ever blocked.
#
# Owners:
#   @souvik-dev-sudo  — Souvik Pal
#   @rahul-qbit       — Rahul Dutta
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Default ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Catch-all. Every path not matched by a later rule lands here.
*                                   @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit


# ── Governance & security policy ──────────────────────────────────────
# Changing the disclosure process, the license, or the conduct policy is a
# project-level decision, not a code change.
/SECURITY.md                        @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/LICENSE                            @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/NOTICE                             @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                 @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit


# ── CI/CD — highest blast radius ──────────────────────────────────────
# These jobs hold the GCP, Firebase, Play and Razorpay credentials. A PR that
# edits a workflow can exfiltrate every secret the job can read, so workflow
# changes always need a second pair of eyes.
/.github/workflows/                 @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/.github/actions/                   @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit

# Secret-scanning config. An allowlist entry here can blind gitleaks to a real
# leak — review every addition against the rules written in the file itself.
/.gitleaks.toml                     @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit

# Automated dependency PRs and the ignore rules that keep secrets out of git.
/.github/dependabot.yml             @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/.gitignore                         @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/.dockerignore                      @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit


# ── Supply chain — lockfiles & manifests ──────────────────────────────
# A lockfile diff is where a typosquatted or backdoored transitive dependency
# actually enters the build. Review the resolved versions, not just the intent.
/pnpm-lock.yaml                     @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/package.json                       @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
**/package.json                     @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
**/package-lock.json                @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/services/chatbot/uv.lock           @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/services/chatbot/requirements.txt  @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit
/services/chatbot/requirements-dev.txt  @souvik-dev-sudo @rahul-qbit


